      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet, because the dose looks like it may be an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The maximum labeled daily dose is 2,550 mg for immediate-release and 2,000 mg for extended-release. This order is about twice that limit, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO BID with meals\n- **500 or 1,000 mg PO BID** with meals, a common titration\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If 1,700 mg TID is intended, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you verified the dose."
      }
